C MP+relacq
"NEGATIVE CONTROL for ra.cat and sra.cat: both models must FORBID this.
 Message passing with a release store and an acquire load. The acquire read of
 the flag synchronises with the release write, so W(x,1) happens-before the read
 of x; reading x=0 then reads an mo-earlier write while aware of an mo-later one,
 which read-coherence forbids in RA and SRA alike. A model that allowed this
 would not be constraining anything, and the 2+2W split would be meaningless."
{ }
P0 (atomic_int* x, atomic_int* f) {
  atomic_store_explicit(x,1,memory_order_release);
  atomic_store_explicit(f,1,memory_order_release);
}
P1 (atomic_int* x, atomic_int* f) {
  int r0 = atomic_load_explicit(f,memory_order_acquire);
  int r1 = atomic_load_explicit(x,memory_order_acquire);
}
exists (1:r0=1 /\ 1:r1=0)
